  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a strong multimodal fusion architecture can achieve high validation accuracy, and which encoder combination is most effective. This experiment tests the core multimodal hypothesis using the strongest available pre-trained encoders (scgpt for RNA, imagenet_vit_l for images) with multiprofile input, avgpool aggregation (simpler and less overfitting-prone than transformer for a first test), and weighted fusion (more flexible than concat for combining heterogeneous modalities). If this performs well, it establishes a strong baseline and direction for exploitation; if it underperforms, it signals that one or more components (encoder choice, fusion strategy, or multimodal integration itself) need simplification, guiding subsequent ablation experiments within the remaining 9-experiment budget."
}

